{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-57804","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67495","text":"SpecPrompt Documentation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67496","marks":["bold"],"text":"Prompts are transient. Specs persist."}]}],"id":"blk-57805","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67497","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-67498","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67499","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-67500","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67501","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-67502","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67503","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-57807","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-57809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67504","text":"Welcome to the documentation hub for "},{"id":"spn-67505","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-67506","text":" — an open standard and toolchain for spec-driven AI development. SpecPrompt defines a Markdown-based specification format (SPEC.md) that is both human-readable and machine-parseable, serving as the source of truth for agent behavior."}]},{"id":"blk-57810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67507","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-67508","marks":["bold"],"text":"standards layer"},{"id":"spn-67509","text":" of the [&] Protocol ecosystem — the format that bridges agent definition with execution, testing, and deployment."}]},{"id":"blk-57811","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67510","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57812","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67511","text":"Why SpecPrompt?"}]},{"id":"blk-57813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67512","text":"Spec-Driven Development (SDD) has emerged as the industry consensus for AI-assisted development in 2026. GitHub Spec Kit, AWS Kiro, Cursor rules, and Next Moca ADL all use different specification formats. Teams switching tools lose context."}]},{"id":"blk-57814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67513","text":"SpecPrompt defines the interoperable standard — a Markdown-native format that is:"}]},{"id":"blk-57815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67514","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-67515","marks":["bold"],"text":"Markdown-native"},{"id":"spn-67516","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-67517","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-67518","text":" files, no proprietary format 2. "},{"id":"spn-67519","marks":["bold"],"text":"Human-first"},{"id":"spn-67520","text":" — readable by any team member, parseable by any agent 3. "},{"id":"spn-67521","marks":["bold"],"text":"Versioned"},{"id":"spn-67522","text":" — lives in git. Branching, diffing, merging. 4. "},{"id":"spn-67523","marks":["bold"],"text":"Testable"},{"id":"spn-67524","text":" — acceptance criteria are machine-executable 5. "},{"id":"spn-67525","marks":["bold"],"text":"Composable"},{"id":"spn-67526","text":" — specs reference other specs 6. "},{"id":"spn-67527","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tool-agnostic"},{"id":"spn-67528","text":" — works with any SDD-compatible tool"}]},{"id":"blk-57816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67529","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57817","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67530","text":"Documentation Map"}]},{"id":"blk-57818","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Homepages\n\n[&] Ampersand Box <https://ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous <https://graphonomous.com>\nBendScript <https://bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems <https://webhost.systems>\nAgentelic <https://agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic <https://agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic <https://delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic <https://deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt <https://fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic <https://geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience <https://opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt <https://specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock <https://ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-57819","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Root Docs\n\n[&] Protocol Docs <https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous Docs <https://docs.graphonomous.com>\nBendScript Docs <https://docs.bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems Docs <https://docs.webhost.systems>\nAgentelic Docs <https://docs.agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic Docs <https://docs.agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic Docs <https://docs.delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic Docs <https://docs.deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt Docs <https://docs.fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic Docs <https://docs.geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience Docs <https://docs.opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt Docs <https://docs.specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock Docs <https://docs.ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-57820","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 2\n:caption: SpecPrompt Docs\n\nspec/README"},{"id":"blk-57821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67531","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57822","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67532","text":"The SPEC.md Format"}]},{"id":"blk-57823","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67533","text":"Every spec follows a structured Markdown format with YAML frontmatter:"}]},{"id":"blk-57824","kind":"code","language":"markdown","text":"---\nname: agent-name\nversion: 1.0.0\nruntime: opensentience | any\nauthor: team-or-person\ncreated: 2026-01-15\nupdated: 2026-02-22\ntags: [category, domain]\ndependencies:\n  - graphonomous\n---\n\n## Purpose\nWhat this agent does and why.\n\n## Capabilities\n- capability:scope (description)\n\n## Constraints\n- Hard and soft behavioral boundaries\n\n## Acceptance Tests\n- Given [precondition] -> [expected behavior]"},{"id":"blk-57825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67534","marks":["bold"],"text":"Required sections:"},{"id":"spn-67535","text":" Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests."}]},{"id":"blk-57826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67536","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57827","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67537","text":"Toolchain"}]},{"id":"blk-57828","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67538","text":"CLI"}]},{"id":"blk-57829","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md      # Validate against format standard\nspecprompt lint SPEC.md          # Check for best practices\nspecprompt test-gen SPEC.md      # Generate test scaffolding\nspecprompt diff SPEC.md@v1 SPEC.md@v2  # Diff two versions\nspecprompt publish SPEC.md       # Publish to FleetPrompt registry"},{"id":"blk-57830","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67539","text":"MCP Tools"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-57832","spans":[{"id":"spn-67540","text":"Tool"}]},{"id":"blk-57833","spans":[{"id":"spn-67541","text":"Description"}]}],"id":"blk-57831","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-57834","spans":[{"id":"spn-67542","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_validate"}]},{"id":"blk-57835","spans":[{"id":"spn-67543","text":"Validate against format standard"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57836","spans":[{"id":"spn-67544","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_lint"}]},{"id":"blk-57837","spans":[{"id":"spn-67545","text":"Check for best practices"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57838","spans":[{"id":"spn-67546","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_generate"}]},{"id":"blk-57839","spans":[{"id":"spn-67547","text":"Generate from natural language"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57840","spans":[{"id":"spn-67548","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_gen"}]},{"id":"blk-57841","spans":[{"id":"spn-67549","text":"Generate test cases from acceptance criteria"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57842","spans":[{"id":"spn-67550","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_diff"}]},{"id":"blk-57843","spans":[{"id":"spn-67551","text":"Compare two spec versions"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57844","spans":[{"id":"spn-67552","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_search"}]},{"id":"blk-57845","spans":[{"id":"spn-67553","text":"Search FleetPrompt registry"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-57846","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67554","text":"Reference Parsers"}]},{"id":"blk-57847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67555","text":"Available in "},{"id":"spn-67556","marks":["bold"],"text":"Elixir"},{"id":"spn-67557","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67558","marks":["bold"],"text":"TypeScript"},{"id":"spn-67559","text":". Formal PEG grammar included in the specification for building conformant parsers."}]},{"id":"blk-57848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67560","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57849","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67561","text":"Ecosystem Integration"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-57851","spans":[{"id":"spn-67562","text":"Product"}]},{"id":"blk-57852","spans":[{"id":"spn-67563","text":"How It Uses SpecPrompt"}]}],"id":"blk-57850","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-57853","spans":[{"id":"spn-67564","marks":["bold"],"text":"Agentelic"}]},{"id":"blk-57854","spans":[{"id":"spn-67565","text":"Specs are the primary input to the build pipeline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57855","spans":[{"id":"spn-67566","marks":["bold"],"text":"OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-57856","spans":[{"id":"spn-67567","text":"Agent manifests reference SPEC.md for permission derivation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57857","spans":[{"id":"spn-67568","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-57858","spans":[{"id":"spn-67569","text":"Learning happens within spec-defined boundaries"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57859","spans":[{"id":"spn-67570","marks":["bold"],"text":"FleetPrompt"}]},{"id":"blk-57860","spans":[{"id":"spn-67571","text":"Specs are published as discoverable templates"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57861","spans":[{"id":"spn-67572","marks":["bold"],"text":"Delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-57862","spans":[{"id":"spn-67573","text":"Multi-agent orchestration specs define agent roles"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-57863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67574","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57864","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67575","text":"Interoperability"}]},{"id":"blk-57865","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67576","marks":["bold"],"text":"AGENTS.md"},{"id":"spn-67577","text":" — complementary (codebase conventions vs. agent behavior specs)"}]}],"id":"blk-57866","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67578","marks":["bold"],"text":"Next Moca ADL"},{"id":"spn-67579","text":" — bidirectional import/export"}]}],"id":"blk-57868","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67580","marks":["bold"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-67581","text":" — bidirectional mapping (capabilities, constraints, governance)"}]}],"id":"blk-57870","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67582","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57873","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67583","text":"Project Links"}]},{"id":"blk-57874","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57876","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67584","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spec:"},{"id":"spn-67585","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67586","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/specprompt.com/docs/spec/README.md"}],"text":"Product Specification"}]}],"id":"blk-57875","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57878","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67587","marks":["bold"],"text":"User stories:"},{"id":"spn-67588","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67589","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/specprompt.com/docs/ux/user-stories.md"}],"text":"SpecPrompt User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-57877","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57880","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67590","marks":["bold"],"text":"Build prompt:"},{"id":"spn-67591","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67592","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/specprompt.com/prompts/BUILD.md"}],"text":"SpecPrompt Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-57879","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67593","marks":["bold"],"text":"[